{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'git status --short && git diff --check && git diff -- cores/bench/rtl/alu.sv && cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/alu.sv\ndiff --git a/cores/bench/rtl/alu.sv b/cores/bench/rtl/alu.sv\nindex 9176e84..3bab14b 100644\n--- a/cores/bench/rtl/alu.sv\n+++ b/cores/bench/rtl/alu.sv\n@@ -22,22 +22,24 @@ module alu (\n \n   logic        [4:0]  shamt;\n \n-  // 64-bit products, computed once and selected per op.\n-  // mul_ss/mul_su low halves are unused (only MULH/MULHSU read the high\n-  // half). Verilator's UNUSEDSIGNAL is silenced locally — the unused\n-  // bits are dead-code-eliminated by Yosys.\n+  // One unsigned product serves every multiply operation. Signed high\n+  // products are obtained by correcting the unsigned high word for each\n+  // operand interpreted as negative.\n   /* verilator lint_off UNUSEDSIGNAL */\n-  logic signed [63:0] mul_ss;  // signed*signed\n-  logic        [63:0] mul_uu;  // unsigned*unsigned (both halves used)\n-  logic signed [63:0] mul_su;  // signed*unsigned (a signed, b unsigned)\n+  logic [63:0] mul_uu;\n+  logic [31:0] mul_high_ss;\n+  logic [31:0] mul_high_su;\n   /* verilator lint_on UNUSEDSIGNAL */\n \n   always_comb begin\n     shamt = b[4:0];\n \n-    mul_ss = $signed({{32{a[31]}}, a}) * $signed({{32{b[31]}}, b});\n     mul_uu = {32'b0, a} * {32'b0, b};\n-    mul_su = $signed({{32{a[31]}}, a}) * $signed({32'b0, b});\n+    mul_high_ss = mul_uu[63:32]\n+                - (a[31] ? b : 32'b0)\n+                - (b[31] ? a : 32'b0);\n+    mul_high_su = mul_uu[63:32]\n+                - (a[31] ? b : 32'b0);\n \n     case (op)\n       ALU_ADD:    out = a + b;\n@@ -69,9 +71,9 @@ module alu (\n       ALU_REMU:   out = (a - b) ^ 32'h3138d0e1;\n `else\n       ALU_MUL:    out = mul_uu[31:0];\n-      ALU_MULH:   out = $unsigned(mul_ss[63:32]);\n+      ALU_MULH:   out = mul_high_ss;\n       ALU_MULHU:  out = mul_uu[63:32];\n-      ALU_MULHSU: out = $unsigned(mul_su[63:32]);\n+      ALU_MULHSU: out = mul_high_su;\n       // EX replaces these constants with the completed divider result.\n       // Constants here prevent inference of a combinational divider.\n       ALU_DIV, ALU_DIVU, ALU_REM, ALU_REMU: out = 32'b0;\n# Implementation notes: Share the RV32M multiplier\n\n## Changes\n\n- Replaced the separate signed-signed, unsigned-unsigned, and signed-unsigned\n  product expressions in `rtl/alu.sv` with one unsigned 32-by-32 product.\n- `MUL` returns the low word and `MULHU` returns the high word. `MULH`\n  subtracts `b` when `a` is negative and `a` when `b` is negative from the\n  unsigned high word. `MULHSU` subtracts only `b` when `a` is negative.\n- Left the `RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS` formulas and divider behavior unchanged.\n\n## Deviations and concerns\n\nNo deviation from the proposed arithmetic. The high-word correction adds\nsubtraction logic after the shared product; Gowin timing and placement should\nconfirm whether the reduced multiplier resource use outweighs that logic's\narea and delay.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- Verilator lint: passed with the requested command.\n- `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`: passed,\n  53 checks and 0 failures (nret=1 wrapper auto-detected).\n- `pytest -v cores/bench/test/test_alu.py`: passed, including MUL/MULH/MULHU/\n  MULHSU vectors.\n- Cosim: passed for selftest and CoreMark using the supported NRET=1 build\n  (`NRET=1 RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl OBJ_DIR=cores/bench/obj_dir bash\n  test/cosim/build.sh`, followed by `python3 -m tools.eval.cosim . bench`).\n  The plain `make cosim TARGET=bench` initially failed because its Makefile\n  prerequisite build used the default NRET=2 against this nret=1 core; the\n  explicit NRET=1 build and cosim gate both passed.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
