{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"git status --short --untracked-files=all && test -f cores/bench/implementation_notes.md && sed -n '1,120p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/core.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv\n# Implementation notes\n\n## Changes\n\n- Replaced the single-PC combinational fetch payload with a four-entry\n  instruction/PC FIFO in `rtl/if_stage.sv`.\n- The fetch PC advances only when `io_imemReady` is high and the response can\n  be accepted. Fetch stalls when the FIFO is full; the backend continues to\n  drain while the FIFO is empty.\n- Decode consumes the FIFO head only when ID/EX can advance. Load-use holds\n  the dependent head while inserting a bubble, and data-memory/divider stalls\n  hold both ID/EX and the queue head.\n- Redirects clear the FIFO and restart fetch at the resolved target. A\n  same-cycle response from the prior fetch address is discarded.\n- Removed imem readiness from the hazard unit. Backend interlocks remain for\n  load-use, data-memory, divider, and redirect conditions.\n\n## Deviations and concerns\n\n- The queue uses registers and a combinational head read. Synthesis may map it\n  to LUTs/flops; the Gowin timing/area flow was not run locally, so the final\n  fitness impact is unmeasured.\n- The FIFO does not bypass an imem response directly to decode when empty,\n  adding a startup cycle before the first instruction can enter ID/EX.\n\n## Local checks\n\n- `verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv +incdir+cores/bench/rtl cores/bench/rtl/*.sv` — passed.\n- `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh` — passed,\n  53 checks and 0 failures. The environment variables are required by the\n  local script invocation.\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench` — passed, both ELF checks. The initial\n  invocation without `NRET=1` used the build script's default `NRET=2`, which\n  does not match this core's `nret: 1` port set.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
