{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_53","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,80p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Implementation notes\n\n## Changes\n\n- Added `rtl/multiplier.sv`, a shared multiplier that registers four unsigned\n  16x16 partial products and combines them with signed-high correction.\n- Removed the ALU's three parallel 32x32 products. The ALU now takes the\n  completed shared-unit result for MUL, MULH, MULHU, and MULHSU.\n- Added multiplier start/busy/done handling alongside the divider. EX holds\n  the multiply instruction for one cycle, then writes the result through the\n  existing EX/MEM and forwarding path. Hazard control stalls IF and ID during\n  that cycle.\n- Added deterministic directed and randomized multiplier tests, updated ALU\n  routing tests, and included the new module in the pipeline test build.\n\n## Deviations and concerns\n\n- ALTOPS mode keeps multiplier start and wait disabled, as it does for the\n  divider, so formal uses the existing abstract M-extension operations.\n- The Gowin timing report for the final RTL measured 41.839 MHz in placement\n  option 0, with 2 DSPs and 22 logic levels. Its worst reported path crosses\n  EX and the divider/control logic, not the partial-product result path. The\n  checked-in core metadata lists 48.326 MHz for the prior snapshot, so this\n  run does not show a Fmax improvement and indicates a timing risk to the\n  hypothesis despite reducing DSP usage.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- Verilator lint: pass.\n- Full bench cocotb unit suite: 7 passed.\n- Formal fast suite: pass, 53 checks using the auto-selected NRET=1 wrapper\n  and checks.\n- Cosimulation: pass, 2 ELF programs tested, with `NRET=1` to match\n  `core.yaml`.\n- Gowin timing: completed; placement option 0 measured 41.839 MHz.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
