{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_58", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,160p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md && sed -n '1,150p' cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv\"", "aggregated_output": "# Implementation notes\n\n## Changes\n\n- Added a one-entry branch tag and target plus a registered lookahead hit in\n  IF. The IF PC mux uses only the registered hit and target; tag comparison\n  computes metadata for the next fetch address.\n- Carried predicted-taken and predicted-target metadata through IF/ID and\n  ID/EX. EX redirects conditional branches when direction or target differs,\n  and restores fall-through if a predicted tag belongs to a non-branch in\n  the current instruction stream.\n- Trained the entry on valid, aligned backward conditional branches. Forward\n  branches do not evict the loop entry. Misaligned branch targets are not\n  predicted.\n\n## Deviations and concerns\n\n- The entry stores only backward branches, matching the loop-target goal\n  while protecting the single entry from forward branches.\n- The saved direction is always taken; a loop exit therefore incurs a\n  direction-mispredict redirect. Dynamic instruction changes at a saved PC\n  are recovered in EX, although normal instruction memories keep the\n  instruction stable.\n- The predictor adds tag, target, and lookahead registers. Gowin placement\n  option 0 reports 44.804 MHz, below the stored baseline figure; the critical\n  path is through forwarding, hazard handling, and ID/EX capture. The full\n  fitness flow and median across placement options have not been run locally.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Verilator lint: passed.\n- Formal: 53 passed, 0 failed after one fix attempt. The first run failed\n  `pc_fwd_ch0` because a tag hit could land on a non-branch in the formal\n  arbitrary instruction stream without EX restoring fall-through. EX now\n  redirects for that case and for speculative misaligned branch targets.\n- Cosimulation: passed all five ELF programs, including stalled and\n  unstalled runs. `make cosim TARGET=bench` by itself defaulted to `NRET=2`\n  and failed to compile; rebuilding with `NRET=1` from `core.yaml` and then\n  running `python3 -m tools.eval.cosim . bench` passed.\n// rtl/if_stage.sv\n//\n// Instruction fetch stage. Holds the PC register\n…[3132 of 6204 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:e0acc25a092d321c]…\nranch_target_q     <= 32'b0;\n      lookahead_hit_q     <= 1'b0;\n      lookahead_target_q  <= 32'b0;\n    end else begin\n      if (branch_train) begin\n        branch_tag_valid_q <= 1'b1;\n        branch_tag_q       <= branch_train_pc;\n        branch_target_q    <= branch_train_target;\n      end\n\n      if (redirect)\n        pc <= redirect_target;\n      else if (!stall)\n        pc <= next_pc;\n\n      // The registered lookup follows sequential fetch only. EX redirect\n      // decisions do not feed either lookahead register; stalls hold the\n      // metadata alongside the held PC.\n      if (!stall) begin\n        lookahead_hit_q <= lookahead_hit_d;\n        lookahead_target_q <= target_for_compare;\n      end\n    end\n  end\n\n  assign imem_addr = pc;\n\n  always_comb begin\n    out.pc    = pc;\n    out.instr = (flush || redirect) ? 32'h0000_0013 : imem_data;\n    out.predicted_taken = lookahead_hit_q && !(flush || redirect);\n    out.predicted_target = lookahead_target_q;\n    out.valid = !(flush || redirect);\n  end\n\nendmodule\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
