{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_32","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'","aggregated_output":"# Implementation notes\n\n## Changes\n\n- IF recognizes branch opcode encodings with legal `funct3` values and a\n  negative B-immediate, computes the target, and selects it for the next PC.\n- Fetch prediction direction and target travel through IF/ID into ID/EX.\n- EX compares the branch outcome and target with the carried prediction. It\n  redirects to the resolved target or fall-through only on a mismatch. A\n  misaligned taken target also redirects to fall-through to recover the\n  speculative fetch; jump behavior and architectural `pc_next` are preserved.\n- `core.sv` includes `core_pkg.sv` so the prescribed wildcard Verilator lint\n  command works even though that glob lists `core.sv` before the package.\n\n## Deviations and concerns\n\nThe predictor uses the instruction's sign bit to identify a negative\nB-immediate after checking the opcode and legal branch `funct3` values. The\nGowin timing run reported 5.272 MHz on placement option 0; its listed critical\npaths remain register-file forwarding through EX/ALU to the memory output.\n\n## Local validation\n\n- Verilator lint: pass.\n- Formal: pass, 53 checks and 0 failures, using `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl`\n  and `CORE_NAME=bench` with automatic `nret: 1` wrapper selection.\n- Cosimulation: pass, 2 ELF images, using `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`.\n  The default `NRET=2` invocation does not match this core's declared\n  single-channel interface.\n- Gowin timing: completed; placement option 0 reported 5.272 MHz.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
