{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,180p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md && git status --short && git diff --check\"","aggregated_output":"# Return stack prediction\n\n## Changes\n\n- Added a four-entry shift-register return stack in IF. The fetch path matches only the exact `jalr x0, x1, 0` encoding and selects the registered top entry directly as the predicted next PC.\n- Carried return prediction valid and target metadata through IF/ID and ID/EX.\n- EX pushes `pc+4` for valid, non-trapping JAL/JALR calls writing x1 or x5. It pops the stack for the exact conventional x1 return only when that instruction advances.\n- EX suppresses a return redirect when the prediction matches the resolved target and redirects on mismatch. If a predicted return resolves to a misaligned target and traps, EX redirects to `pc+4` to recover the speculative IF PC.\n\n## Deviations and concerns\n\n- Calls are recognized through either link register x1 or x5; prediction remains limited to x1 returns as proposed.\n- The stack drops its oldest entry on overflow. x5 returns and other JALR forms use the normal redirect path.\n- A return target comparison remains in EX, and the added state increases area. The timing result below is one placement option, so the scored median Fmax and net fitness still need evaluation.\n\n## Local checks\n\n- Verilator lint: pass.\n- Formal: first run found a `pc_fwd_ch0` counterexample where a predicted return target was misaligned; added sequential-PC recovery for that trapping case. Rerun passed all 53 checks.\n- Cosim: `make cosim TARGET=bench` used the build script's default NRET=2 and failed to compile against this NRET=1 core. `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench` passed both selftest and CoreMark.\n- Gowin timing: placement option 0 reported 42.029 MHz and 21 logic levels. This is a single-option measurement, not the evaluator's median.\n M cores/bench/rtl/core.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_37","type":"agent_message","text":"Implemented the four-entry return stack in IF, carried prediction metadata through ID/EX, and added EX push, pop, match, and misprediction recovery logic. Notes are in [implementation_notes.md](/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6-luna_xhigh-v2-rep6/cores/bench/implementation_notes.md).\n\nLint passed, formal passed all 53 checks, and cosim passed selftest and CoreMark with `NRET=1`. The default cosim command used NRET=2 and failed to compile against this NRET=1 core. Gowin timing option 0 reported 42.029 MHz; the scored median remains to be evaluated."}}
