{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_40","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat implementation_notes.md && git diff --check --no-index /dev/null implementation_notes.md || true'","aggregated_output":"# Implementation notes\n\n## Changes\n\n- IF recognizes the legal RV32I JAL opcode, reconstructs its signed J immediate, and computes `PC + immediate`. It selects that target for the next fetch PC only when the target is 4-byte aligned.\n- The IF/ID and ID/EX payloads carry a prediction-valid bit and target. EX suppresses the redirect for a direct JAL only when that carried target equals the resolved jump target. Other jumps, mismatches, and misaligned-target traps retain the existing handling.\n- No unit-test files were changed.\n\n## Deviations and concerns\n\n- The metadata is carried through the existing IF/ID combinational bundle and ID/EX register; no separate prediction stage or table was added.\n- The fetch target adder adds area and could affect timing. Gowin measured 43.874 MHz median Fmax, 2694 logic cells, and 631 registers. The critical path reported by placement 0 still runs through register-file and EX logic.\n- This core declares `nret: 1`, while the local Make targets default the cosim build macro to NRET=2. I ran the checks with `NRET=1`; no build or harness files were changed.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- Verilator lint: pass.\n- Formal: pass, 53 checks, using `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh` (which auto-selects the single-issue wrapper/config).\n- Cosim: pass, 5 ELF runs, with and without memory stalls, using `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`.\n- FPGA evaluation: pass. CoreMark completed 10 iterations in 4,442,158 cycles with the expected validation output; reported fitness was 98.77 iter/s.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_41","type":"agent_message","text":"Implemented direct JAL prediction in [if_stage.sv](/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6-luna_xhigh-v2-rep6/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261001-003-r6s2/cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv), carried the target through ID/EX, and suppressed EX redirects for matching predictions.\n\n- Lint passed; formal passed (53 checks).\n- Cosim passed (5 ELF runs) with `NRET=1`.\n- FPGA evaluation passed: 43.874 MHz median Fmax, 4,442,158 CoreMark cycles, fitness 98.77 iter/s.\n- Details are in [implementation_notes.md](/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6-luna_xhigh-v2-rep6/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261001-003-r6s2/implementation_notes.md)."}}
