{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_35","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"git diff --check && git status --short && sed -n '1,120p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/core.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv\n# Implementation notes: single-entry loop branch predictor\n\n## Changes\n\n- Added one valid bit, full PC tag, resolved target, and 2-bit saturating direction counter in IF.\n- EX trains the entry from valid, aligned backward conditional branches as they advance out of EX. A new entry starts weakly in the direction just observed.\n- Carried prediction-valid, direction, and target metadata from IF through ID/EX. Conditional branches redirect on a direction or predicted-target mismatch; jumps still redirect unconditionally.\n- Qualified predictor hits with the current fetched opcode and legal branch funct3 values. The formal wrapper supplies a new symbolic instruction each cycle rather than an address-indexed instruction memory, so a PC tag alone could otherwise steer fetch for a non-branch instruction. EX also checks the saved target and corrects target mismatches.\n\n## Checks\n\n- Verilator lint: pass with `-Wall`.\n- Formal: first run failed the branch instruction checks and PC-forward check because the unqualified tag hit acted on arbitrary symbolic fetch instructions. Added IF branch qualification; the second run passed all 53 checks.\n- Co-simulation: `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench` passed both selftest and CoreMark. The initial default `NRET=2` invocation failed to compile because this core declares `nret: 1` and has no channel-1 ports.\n- Gowin timing: 43.887 MHz for placement option 0, 20 logic levels. The worst reported path starts at the register file and ends in the ID/EX operand register, through EX, IF, and hazard control. This measurement alone does not establish the net CoreMark fitness change.\n\n## Concerns\n\n- IF now has a small opcode/funct3 qualification cone on the predictor select path. It does not generate the immediate or add the target on a predicted-taken fetch.\n- A single entry is replaced by each distinct backward conditional branch, so workloads alternating among loop branches can evict useful targets.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"agent_message","text":"Implemented the single-entry backward-branch predictor. IF carries prediction metadata to EX; EX trains the tagged target and saturating counter, and corrects direction or target mismatches. IF checks the fetched instruction is a legal branch before using a hit, which is needed for the formal wrapper’s symbolic instruction stream.\n\n**Checks:** Verilator lint passed; formal passed all 53 checks after that qualification fix; `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench` passed selftest and CoreMark. Gowin timing measured 43.887 MHz for placement option 0; that alone does not establish the net fitness change. The initial cosim command used the wrong default `NRET=2` for this `nret: 1` core.\n\nNotes: [implementation_notes.md](/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6-luna_xhigh-v2-rep6/cores/bench/implementation_notes.md)"}}
