{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_3", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'tail -n 8 cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl && git status --short && git log -4 --oneline -- cores/bench/rtl/core.sv'", "aggregated_output": "{\"id\": \"hyp-20261001-003-r9s2\", \"title\": \"Shared loop direction predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"Prior predictor attempts lost fitness to indexed lookups, target storage,\\nfetch-side return selection, or early branch resolution. A compact shared\\ndirection state may learn recurring loop behavior with less logic than a\\nbranch-indexed table, while limiting predictions to backward branches.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"Prior predictor attempts lost fitness to indexed lookups, target storage,\\nfetch-side return selection, or early branch resolution. A compact shared\\ndirection state may learn recurring loop behavior with less logic than a\\nbranch-indexed table, while limiting predictions to backward branches.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add one global two-bit saturating counter, initialized weakly taken and\\nupdated by each resolved conditional branch. In fetch, only legal backward\\nconditional branches consult this counter; when it predicts taken, use the\\nbranch immediate target, and otherwise continue sequentially. Carry the\\nprediction bit with the instruction and have EX redirect only when the\\nactual outcome differs. The shared state removes table indexing and tag\\ncomparisons from the predictor while adapting to loop exits, which may\\nimprove on fixed backward-taken prediction without the area and lookup cost\\nof multi-entry direction tables.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Carry predicted branch direction from fetch through ID/EX.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a shared saturating direction counter and use it for backward b