{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_2", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl && cat cores/bench/core.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "{\"id\": \"baseline-bench-a1886e3\", \"title\": \"Baseline retest for cores/bench\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 12.12, \"delta_pct\": 0.0, \"vs_baseline\": 0.0, \"fmax_mhz\": 5.442, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 12312, \"ff\": 460, \"seeds\": [5.14, 5.442, 5.442], \"perturbations\": [[0, 5.14, 150], [1, 5.442, 149], [2, 5.442, 149]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_3_s0\", \"to\": \"dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -189.542, \"arrival_ns\": 199.837, \"logic_cells\": 156, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_fwd\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 150, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T02:57:32.974071Z\", \"round_id\": 0, \"slot\": 0}\n{\"id\": \"hyp-20261001-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"One-hot forwarding bypass\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The recorded worst path runs from a MEM/WB destination register through the forwarding unit and EX ALU to the data-memory address. Binary forwarding selection adds selector encoding and data-mux logic to this path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The recorded worst path runs from a MEM/WB destination register through the forwarding unit and EX ALU to the data-memory address. Binary forwarding selection adds selector encoding and data-mux logic to this path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Generate priority-correct one-hot hits for the register-file, EX/MEM, and MEM/WB operands, then combine masked operand values in EX with an OR. This removes the binary select decode between register-tag comparison and ALU input, which may shorten the critical forwarding-to-address path.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 7, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Produce one-hot operand-source selects while preserving EX/MEM-over-MEM/WB priority and x0 behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace the binary case forwarding muxes with one-hot\n…[82118 of 85190 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:11cdae9ccbe33d34]…\nlogic_levels\": 20, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T06:28:58.060744Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 9, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-001-r9s0 (regression, -3.39%): Four 8-bit carry-select blocks duplicate upper `a+b` and `a+b+1` arithmetic yet retain a block-to-block carry selection chain, so extra muxing and routing can outweigh reduced bit-level carry depth on the ALU effective-address path.\"}\nname: bench\ndescription: Frozen LLM-benchmark fixture core. Identical RTL to baseline at the bench-fixture-v1\n  freeze point. The benchmark matrix clones from the bench-fixture-v1 orphan branch\n  and operates only on this directory.\nisa: rv32im\nnret: 1\ntarget_fpga: tang-nano-20k\ntargets:\n  fmax_mhz: 135\n  lut4: 10000\n  coremark_iter_s: 300\n  coremark_per_mhz: 2.2\ncurrent:\n  fmax_mhz: 48.326\n  lut4: 2479\n  ff: 600\n  coremark_iter_s: 2.0e-06\n  coremark_per_mhz: 0.0\n  source_id: hyp-20261001-002-r1s1\n  updated: '2026-10-01T03:20:41.566166Z'\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
