{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_3", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg 'hyp-20261001-002-r9s1|hyp-20261001-002-r6s1|\\\"title\\\": \\\"Shared' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "{\"id\": \"hyp-20261001-002-r6s1\", \"title\": \"Pipeline the multiplier partial products\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"Recent timing reports still show paths through EX and the ALU, while the current ALU evaluates three full-width 32x32 products in parallel for the M-extension multiply variants. Those wide multiplier cones consume DSP resources and can dominate the clock period even though only one result is selected.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"Recent timing reports still show paths through EX and the ALU, while the current ALU evaluates three full-width 32x32 products in parallel for the M-extension multiply variants. Those wide multiplier cones consume DSP resources and can dominate the clock period even though only one result is selected.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the parallel full-width products with a shared two-stage partial-product multiplier. Compute and register four 16x16 partial products in the first stage, then combine them and apply signed-high correction in the second stage. Hold the multiply instruction for one extra cycle and release its result through the normal EX/MEM forwarding path. Shorter multiplier stages should improve Fmax, while the small per-MUL latency penalty should be limited on CoreMark and the shared unit should reduce DSP pressure. Preserve exact MUL, MULH, MULHU, and MULHSU results.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 9, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove the three parallel full-width products and route all multiply variants through the staged shared multiplier result.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/multiplier.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a two-stage 16x16 partial-product unit with correct signed and unsigned high-half results.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Start multiply operations, hold the instruction for the extra stage, and send the completed result through EX/MEM.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Connect multiplier start, busy, and completion control alongside the existing divider interface.\"},\n…[1026 of 4098 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:659a3c6ad4bb959a]…\n \"regression\", \"fitness\": 95.04, \"delta_pct\": -11.66, \"vs_baseline\": 684.16, \"fmax_mhz\": 43.578, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4585414, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 2879, \"ff\": 671, \"seeds\": [41.839, 43.578, 43.578], \"perturbations\": [[0, 41.839, 22], [1, 43.578, 23], [2, 43.578, 23]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 2, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_id/id_ex_w.rs2_val_8_s1\", \"slack_ns\": -18.901, \"arrival_ns\": 29.196, \"logic_cells\": 44, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_divider\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_if\", \"cpu/u_hazard\", \"cpu/u_id\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 22, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T05:32:46.516001Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 6, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-002-r6s1 (regression, -11.66%): A shared two-stage multiplier holds this in-order EX stage for an extra cycle on each multiply, so its per-operation latency can outweigh shorter multiplier logic on CoreMark.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
