', 'cpu/u_rf'] | - 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-001-r5s0 (regression, -12.18%): Explicitly staging each async register-file read as eight replicated 4:1 selections followed by an 8:1 mux worsened fitness, suggesting the low-address select fanout and routing can outweigh local mux sizing on this FPGA.\nhyp-20261001-001-r6s0 | Mask uninitialized register-file storage | regression | -4.01 | ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_divider', 'cpu/u_if', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_if', 'cpu/u_hazard', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_if'] | - 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-001-r6s0 (regression, -4.01%): Per-register validi\n…[1772 of 4844 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:cf32c1e350d24888]…\nin.\nhyp-20261001-001-r11s0 | Retiming signed divider normalization | regression | -2.01 | ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex'] | - 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-001-r11s0 (regression, -2.01%): The new init cycle adds latency to every signed DIV/REM with a negative operand, so launch-path retiming must earn back that per-operation cost in measured timing on CoreMark.\nhyp-20261001-001-r12s0 | Remove fetch bubble mux from hazard feedback | regression | -4.06 | ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex'] | \nhyp-20261001-001-r13s0 | Qualify load-use hazards by operand use | regression | -5.04 | ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_divider', 'cpu/u_if', 'cpu/u_hazard', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_if', 'cpu/u_id'] | - 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-001-r13s0 (regression, -5.04%): Opcode-qualified load-use checks can remove false stalls, but adding two asynchronous register-file read ports to preserve RVFI source snapshots can cost more than those bubbles save on CoreMark.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 -c 'import json; rows=[json.loads(x) for x in open(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\\\")];\nfor r in rows:\n if r.get(\\\"id\\\") in (\\\"hyp-20261001-001-r7s0\\\",\\\"hyp-20261001-001-r12s0\\\",\\\"hyp-20261001-001-r3s0\\\",\\\"hyp-20261001-002-r10s1\\\"):\n  print(\\\"ID\\\",r.get(\\\"id\\\"),\\\"TITLE\\\",r.get(\\\"title\\\")); h=r.get(\\\"hypothesis\\\",{}); print(\\\"HYP\\\",h.get(\\\"hypothesis\\\",\\\"\\\")); print(\\\"NOTES\\\",r.get(\\\"implementation_notes\\\",\\\"\\\")); print(\\\"PATH\\\",r.get(\\\"critical_path\\\")); print()'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 -c 'import json; rows=[json.loads(x) for x in open(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\\\")];\nfor r in rows:\n if r.get(\\\"id\\\") in (\\\"hyp-20261001-001-r7s0\\\",\\\"hyp-20261001-001-r12s0\\\",\\\"hyp-20261001-001-r3s0\\\",\\\"hyp-20261001-002-r10s1\\\"):\n  print(\\\"ID\\\",r.get(\\\"id\\\"),\\\"TITLE\\\",r.get(\\\"title\\\")); h=r.get(\\\"hypothesis\\\",{}); print(\\\"HYP\\\",h.get(\\\"hypothesis\\\",\\\"\\\")); print(\\\"NOTES\\\",r.get(\\\"implementation_notes\\\",\\\"\\\")); print(\\\"PATH\\\",r.get(\\\"critical_path\\\")); print()'\"","aggregated_output":"ID hyp-20261001-001-r3s0 TITLE Share the RV32M multiplier\nHYP Compute one unsigned 32-by-32 product for all multiply instructions. MUL\nuses its low word directly; MULHU uses its high word directly; MULHSU and\nMULH correct that high word by subtracting the appropriate sign-dependent\noperand terms. This preserves single-cycle multiply behavior and RV32M\nresults while removing redundant multiplier hardware, potentially freeing\nDSP and routing resources for a better placed, faster netlist.\n\nNOTES \nPATH {'from': 'cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0', 'to': 'dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -18.878, 'arrival_ns': 29.173, 'logic_cells': 22, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\n\nID hyp-20261001-001-r7s0 TITLE Bypass ALU selection for memory addresses\nHYP Add a dedicated effective-address sum from the already-forwarded rs1 value and the decoded immediate, and select that sum into EX/MEM for loads and stores. This removes the AUIPC/operand muxes and general ALU result selection from the memory-address path while leaving the existing ALU operations and their results unchanged for non-memory instructions. The extra adder uses available LUT headroom and targets the repeatedly observed EX-to-address timing bottleneck without changing pipeline latency or memory semantics.\n\nNOTES \nPATH {'from': 'cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_id/id_ex_w.rs2_val_4_s1', 'slack_ns': -15.703, 'arrival_ns': 25.998, 'logic_cells': 39, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_divider', 'cpu/u_if', 'cpu/u_hazard', 'cpu/u_id']}\n\nID hyp-20261001-002-r10s1 TITLE Detach divide execution from decode hold\nHYP Give the iterative divider a dedicated execution context that captures the full DIV/REM instruction metadata and forwarded operands when the operation starts. Replace the ID/EX instruction with a bubble while the divider runs, and have EX/MEM accept the captured instruction with the completed result when done. Keep fetch held and suppress decode capture during the operation so no younger instruction is lost or duplicated. This preserves precise in-order retirement while removing the divider wait signal from the ID/EX hold mux, which should shorten the current critical control path.\n\nNOTES \nPATH {'from': 'cpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_0_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_id/id_ex_w.rs1_val_0_s100', 'slack_ns': -15.791, 'arrival_ns': 26.085, 'logic_cells': 47, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_fwd', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_divider', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_if', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_if', 'cpu/u_hazard', 'cpu/u_id']}\n\nID hyp-20261001-001-r12s0 TITLE Remove fetch bubble mux from hazard feedback\nHYP Keep the fetched instruction word unmodified in the IF/ID bundle and use its valid bit to gate load-use detection. At the ID/EX boundary, capture a bubble whenever the incoming fetch payload is invalid, while preserving the existing hold priority during data-memory stalls. This removes the redirect and fetch-stall controlled 32-bit NOP mux from the IF-to-hazard path, potentially improving Fmax without changing issue or retirement timing.\n\nNOTES \nPATH {'from': 'cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0', 'to': 'dmem_1_dmem_1_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -15.722, 'arrival_ns': 26.016, 'logic_cells': 13, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
