{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-001-r14s0.yaml && sed -n '1,240p' schemas/hypothesis.schema.json\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261001-001-r14s0\ntitle: \"Retiming memory address addition into MEM\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The recurring critical path starts at the register file and passes through forwarding, EX, and the ALU before reaching the data-memory address. The existing dedicated-address-adder attempt still placed forwarding and address addition in the same stage, leaving their delays combined.\nhypothesis: |\n  Carry the forwarded base register value and immediate through EX/MEM, then form load/store effective addresses in MEM. This places the EX/MEM register between the forwarding mux and address adder, shortening the long register-file-to-memory-output path while retaining the existing single-cycle memory interface. Use the resulting address consistently for misalignment checks, byte lanes, dmem requests, and RVFI aligned memory reporting.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 7\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add an immediate field to the EX/MEM payload for deferred load/store address calculation.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Capture the forwarded base and immediate in EX/MEM while preserving existing non-memory ALU results and divider completion.\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Calculate effective memory addresses from registered base-plus-immediate and use them for bus outputs, alignment, byte masks, and RVFI memory fields.\"\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"required\": [\"id\",\"title\",\"category\",\"motivation\",\"hypothesis\",\"expected_impact\",\"changes\"],\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"id\":       {\"type\": \"string\", \"pattern\": \"^hyp-[0-9]{8}-[0-9]{3}(-r[0-9]+s[0-9]+)?$\"},\n    \"title\":    {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 5},\n    \"category\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"micro_opt\",\"structural\",\"extension\",\"predictor\",\"memory\"]},\n    \"motivation\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"hypothesis\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"expected_impact\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"required\": [\"fitness_delta_pct\",\"confidence\"],\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"fitness_delta_pct\": {\"type\": \"integer\"},\n        \"confidence\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"low\",\"medium\",\"high\"]}\n      }\n    },\n    \"changes\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\", \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"required\": [\"file\",\"description\"],\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"file\":        {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"Must be under rtl/ (any extension) or be a test/test_*.py cocotb suite. Anything else is rejected by the runtime sandbox check.\",\n            \"pattern\": \"^(rtl/[^.].*|test/test_[^/]+\\\\.py)$\"\n          },\n          \"description\": {\"type\": \"string\"}\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
