{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 -c 'import json; rows=[json.loads(x) for x in open(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\\\")];\nfor r in rows:\n if r.get(\\\"id\\\") in [\\\"hyp-20261001-001-r4s0\\\",\\\"hyp-20261001-001-r5s0\\\",\\\"hyp-20261001-001-r7s0\\\",\\\"hyp-20261001-001-r10s0\\\"]:\n  print(\\\"\\\\n###\\\",r[\\\"id\\\"],r[\\\"title\\\"]); print(r.get(\\\"hypothesis\\\",{}).get(\\\"hypothesis\\\")); print(r.get(\\\"implementation_notes\\\"))' \"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 -c 'import json; rows=[json.loads(x) for x in open(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\\\")];\nfor r in rows:\n if r.get(\\\"id\\\") in [\\\"hyp-20261001-001-r4s0\\\",\\\"hyp-20261001-001-r5s0\\\",\\\"hyp-20261001-001-r7s0\\\",\\\"hyp-20261001-001-r10s0\\\"]:\n  print(\\\"\\\\n###\\\",r[\\\"id\\\"],r[\\\"title\\\"]); print(r.get(\\\"hypothesis\\\",{}).get(\\\"hypothesis\\\")); print(r.get(\\\"implementation_notes\\\"))' \"","aggregated_output":"\n### hyp-20261001-001-r4s0 Bank the register-file read mux\nReplace each flat 32-entry asynchronous read with a four-bank, eight-register mux: select within each bank using the low address bits, then select a bank using the high bits. Keep x0 reads and same-cycle WB write-first bypass behavior exact. A staged mux topology may map to shallower local LUT logic and reduce read-select fanout, improving Fmax without adding a pipeline cycle or changing instruction timing.\n\n\n\n### hyp-20261001-001-r5s0 Rebalance the register-file read mux\nReorganize both register-file read ports into eight banks of four registers, selecting one of four words locally before selecting among the eight bank results. Preserve the x0 constant and same-cycle write-first bypass behavior. This changes only the mux grouping, retaining the existing pipeline and instruction timing, while aiming to reduce LUT depth and routing on the current read-path bottleneck.\n\n\n\n### hyp-20261001-001-r7s0 Bypass ALU selection for memory addresses\nAdd a dedicated effective-address sum from the already-forwarded rs1 value and the decoded immediate, and select that sum into EX/MEM for loads and stores. This removes the AUIPC/operand muxes and general ALU result selection from the memory-address path while leaving the existing ALU operations and their results unchanged for non-memory instructions. The extra adder uses available LUT headroom and targets the repeatedly observed EX-to-address timing bottleneck without changing pipeline latency or memory semantics.\n\n\n\n### hyp-20261001-001-r10s0 Register divider terminal-cycle decode\nRegister a final-cycle flag when the divider advances from count 30 to count 31, then drive `done` directly from that flag. This moves the terminal-count comparison off the same-cycle divider-to-stall-release path while keeping the 32-step recurrence, completion cycle, and result selection unchanged. It should shorten the recurring control path without changing ordinary instruction latency or arithmetic behavior.\n\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
