{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-001-r7s0.yaml && git status --short'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261001-001-r7s0\ntitle: \"Bypass ALU selection for memory addresses\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  Recent timing reports repeatedly place the critical endpoint in the EX ALU, including the data-memory address path. A load or store always adds its forwarded base register to its immediate, but currently passes through the general ALU operand selection and operation-result selection used by every instruction.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a dedicated effective-address sum from the already-forwarded rs1 value and the decoded immediate, and select that sum into EX/MEM for loads and stores. This removes the AUIPC/operand muxes and general ALU result selection from the memory-address path while leaving the existing ALU operations and their results unchanged for non-memory instructions. The extra adder uses available LUT headroom and targets the repeatedly observed EX-to-address timing bottleneck without changing pipeline latency or memory semantics.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Compute forwarded base plus immediate on a dedicated memory-address path and select it for load/store EX results.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
