{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_8", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'structural' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | tail -50\"", "aggregated_output": "3:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261001-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Iterative shared divider\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The measured critical path runs through forwarding, EX, and the ALU, and the current ALU contains four combinational divide/remainder operators. Their long arithmetic cones can dominate timing even when the current instruction is not a divide.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The measured critical path runs through forwarding, EX, and the ALU, and the current ALU contains four combinational divide/remainder operators. Their long arithmetic cones can dominate timing even when the current instruction is not a divide.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Move DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU into a shared radix-2 iterative execution unit that performs one quotient bit per cycle. Interlock the in-order pipeline while the unit runs and return the completed quotient or remainder through EX/MEM. This removes the deep combinational divider from the ordinary EX datapath, which should raise Fmax substantially; the cycle penalty is limited to divide/remainder instructions. Preserve RV32M corner cases, including divide by zero and signed overflow.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 12, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove combinational divide and remainder operators from the main ALU path and route these operations to the iterative unit.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Start and collect iterative divide/remainder operations while holding the executing instruction until its result is ready.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Coordinate divider busy/complete interlocking with fetch, decode, and downstream pipeline state.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"