{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"The structural history has two useful clues: the current worst path crosses the register file, execute, divider, fetch, and hazard logic; a fetch/decode register by itself regressed slightly. I’ll propose a synchronous-read register file with matching pipeline alignment, aimed at placing a clock boundary before that long operand path."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"mkdir -p cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses && cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-002-r12s1.yaml <<'EOF'\nid: hyp-20261001-002-r12s1\ntitle: \\\"Synchronous register-file read stage\\\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The measured critical path starts at a register-file bit and continues through\n  ID, forwarding, EX, divider control, fetch, and hazard feedback. The prior\n  fetch/decode register alone did not improve fitness, so the operand read itself\n  needs a real clock boundary to break the long combinational chain.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the asynchronous two-port register-file read with duplicated\n  synchronous-read memories, one copy per read port, and align fetched\n  instruction metadata with the registered read results. A registered memory\n  read can map to the FPGA's embedded RAM and prevents register-file selection\n  logic from feeding through EX and back into fetch/decode control in one cycle.\n  Preserve x0, reset-to-zero behavior, WB collision bypass, in-order issue, and\n  load-use/redirect correctness while keeping one instruction per cycle after\n  the pipeline fills. The added boundary should raise Fmax enough to offset the\n  extra redirect and startup latency on CoreMark.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/reg_file.sv\n    description: \\\"Use duplicated synchronous-read storage for the two source ports, retaining x0 semantics, reset-visible zeros, and correct WB collision forwarding.\\\"\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \\\"Add the fetch/decode metadata needed to keep instruction state aligned with registered register-file read data.\\\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \\\"Register fetched instruction and PC across the new synchronous-read boundary while preserving redirect and imem-stall behavior.\\\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \\\"Align decoded controls and source addresses with registered read values at the execute input.\\\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \\\"Adapt load-use, forwarding, flush, and stall control for the added fetch/read boundary.\\\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \\\"Connect the retimed fetch, register-file, and execute boundaries without changing the nret=1 top-level contract.\\\"\nEOF\n\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
