S (secs)]: 0:00:01 (1)\nSBY  9:22:09 [insn_xor_ch0] summary: Elapsed process time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:01 (1)\nSBY  9:22:09 [insn_xor_ch0] summary: engine_0 (smtbmc bitwuzla) returned pass\nSBY  9:22:09 [insn_xor_ch0] summary: engine_0 did not produce any traces\nSBY  9:22:09 [insn_xor_ch0] DONE (PASS, rc=0)\nSBY  9:22:09 [insn_xori_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:00  Status: passed\nSBY  9:22:09 [insn_xori_ch0] engine_0: finished (returncode=0)\nSBY  9:22:09 [insn_xori_ch0] engine_0: Status returned by engine: pass\nSBY  9:22:09 [insn_xori_ch0] summary: Elapsed clock time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:01 (1)\nSBY  9:22:09 [insn_xori_ch0] summary: Elapsed process time [H:MM:SS\n…[3054 of 6126 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:d0e3f26694c2593a]…\nry address. That combines register matching, a 32-bit operand mux, and arithmetic in one cycle. A pipeline boundary between operand selection and execution can shorten this path while retaining one instruction per cycle in the steady state.\n\nhypothesis: Divide EX into an operand-capture stage and an execute stage. Resolve and register operands at the new boundary, including a bypass from the concurrently executing older instruction's result and the existing writeback value, so the arithmetic stage does not repeat the long producer comparisons and forwarding muxes. Extend interlocks for loads and other unavailable results, flush the younger captured instruction on redirects, and preserve detached DIV/REM completion and in-order retirement. This should raise Fmax enough to outweigh the added branch recovery latency. The prior split-EX attempt failed its register check because it did not account for dependencies across the new producer stage; the bypass and stall rules must explicitly cover those dependencies.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
