{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-002-r4s1.yaml && cat schemas/hypothesis.schema.json && git status --short'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261001-002-r4s1\ntitle: \"Decouple stores with a one-entry buffer\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The benchmark injects dmem stalls on roughly 22% of cycles, and the current\n  pipeline freezes behind every stalled store. A store can wait for the bus\n  independently of the next arithmetic instructions, so this stall need not\n  immediately stop issue. The existing critical control path also crosses\n  memory backpressure logic.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a one-entry posted-store buffer at the MEM boundary. When a store reaches\n  MEM and the buffer is empty, let the pipeline advance while the buffer holds\n  its aligned address, replicated write data, and byte enables until dmemReady\n  accepts the request. Keep the buffered request stable under backpressure.\n  Stall a later store only when the buffer is occupied, and hold a load at MEM\n  until all older buffered stores drain so memory ordering and load-after-store\n  behavior remain precise. This should hide isolated store wait cycles behind\n  independent execution, improving CoreMark iterations per cycle without\n  adding lookup logic to the fetch or ALU paths.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add a one-entry pending-store buffer, stable bus request selection, enqueue/dequeue handling, and load ordering interlock.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Connect the MEM buffer's backpressure and ordering status to pipeline stall control.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Advance independent instructions behind a buffered store while holding accesses that cannot yet be accepted safely.\"\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"required\": [\"id\",\"title\",\"category\",\"motivation\",\"hypothesis\",\"expected_impact\",\"changes\"],\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"id\":       {\"type\": \"string\", \"pattern\": \"^hyp-[0-9]{8}-[0-9]{3}(-r[0-9]+s[0-9]+)?$\"},\n    \"title\":    {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 5},\n    \"category\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"micro_opt\",\"structural\",\"extension\",\"predictor\",\"memory\"]},\n    \"motivation\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"hypothesis\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"expected_impact\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"required\": [\"fitness_delta_pct\",\"confidence\"],\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"fitness_delta_pct\": {\"type\": \"integer\"},\n        \"confidence\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"low\",\"medium\",\"high\"]}\n      }\n    },\n    \"changes\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\", \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"required\": [\"file\",\"description\"],\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"file\":        {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"Must be under rtl/ (any extension) or be a test/test_*.py cocotb suite. Anything else is rejected by the runtime sandbox check.\",\n            \"pattern\": \"^(rtl/[^.].*|test/test_[^/]+\\\\.py)$\"\n          },\n          \"description\": {\"type\": \"string\"}\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
