{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-002-r5s1.yaml && git status --short -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-002-r5s1.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261001-002-r5s1\ntitle: \"Decouple fetch with an instruction queue\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The current hazard logic turns every imemReady gap into a whole-pipeline stall. With randomized instruction and data bus stalls, this can stop older independent work and forces fetch readiness into the pipeline control path. A small queue can collect instructions while the backend is blocked and let execution continue through later fetch gaps.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a four-entry instruction queue between fetch and decode, with a fetch PC that advances only when an instruction is accepted. Enqueue valid imem responses independently while decode is held by a data-memory or divider stall; consume queued instructions whenever decode can advance. When the queue is empty, inject a bubble and allow older pipeline stages to drain instead of freezing the whole core. Flush queued wrong-path instructions and restart fetch at the resolved redirect target. This should hide some randomized imem stalls behind backend wait periods and remove imemReady from the global stall decision, improving CoreMark throughput and shortening the fetch-to-hazard control path.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add a small instruction-and-PC queue, independent enqueue/fetch control, dequeue signaling, and redirect flushing.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Connect queue availability and consumption to decode while separating instruction fetch readiness from backend pipeline stalls.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Remove imemReady from whole-pipeline stall generation and preserve load-use, data-memory, divider, and redirect interlocks with queue-empty bubbles.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
