{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-002-r6s1.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261001-002-r6s1\ntitle: \"Pipeline the multiplier partial products\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  Recent timing reports still show paths through EX and the ALU, while the current ALU evaluates three full-width 32x32 products in parallel for the M-extension multiply variants. Those wide multiplier cones consume DSP resources and can dominate the clock period even though only one result is selected.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the parallel full-width products with a shared two-stage partial-product multiplier. Compute and register four 16x16 partial products in the first stage, then combine them and apply signed-high correction in the second stage. Hold the multiply instruction for one extra cycle and release its result through the normal EX/MEM forwarding path. Shorter multiplier stages should improve Fmax, while the small per-MUL latency penalty should be limited on CoreMark and the shared unit should reduce DSP pressure. Preserve exact MUL, MULH, MULHU, and MULHSU results.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 9\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: Remove the three parallel full-width products and route all multiply variants through the staged shared multiplier result.\n  - file: rtl/multiplier.sv\n    description: Add a two-stage 16x16 partial-product unit with correct signed and unsigned high-half results.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: Start multiply operations, hold the instruction for the extra stage, and send the completed result through EX/MEM.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: Connect multiplier start, busy, and completion control alongside the existing divider interface.\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: Interlock fetch and decode during staged multiplication while allowing older pipeline work to advance safely.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
