{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-002-r8s1.yaml && git status --short -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-002-r8s1.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261001-002-r8s1\ntitle: \"Register the fetch/decode boundary\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The recurring critical path spans register-file operands, EX control, fetch, hazard logic, and the ID/EX input. The current frontend has no registered IF/ID boundary: fetched instruction data and EX-driven redirect or stall qualification feed decode in the same cycle. A pipeline register at this boundary can isolate frontend fetch control from decode and operand capture.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add an explicit IF/ID register that captures instruction, PC, and validity when an instruction fetch completes. Decode consumes this registered payload while fetch independently advances or holds its PC. On redirects, invalidate buffered younger instructions and capture the target-path instruction only after the redirect; preserve exact instruction order across imem stalls, load-use stalls, divider waits, and dmem stalls. This adds frontend control and may add a redirect bubble, but it should shorten the repeated EX-to-fetch-to-decode feedback path enough to improve Fmax without adding latency to ordinary ALU execution.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Define the registered IF/ID payload carrying PC, instruction, and validity.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Capture completed fetches in an IF/ID register and handle PC hold, redirects, and frontend invalidation.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Decode the registered IF/ID instruction and preserve existing ID/EX stall and flush behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the registered fetch/decode boundary and retain the single-channel RVFI retirement contract.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Coordinate the buffered frontend with imem stalls, load-use hazards, redirects, divider waits, and dmem stalls.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
