{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_1", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg 'category: structural|structural' experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "{\"id\": \"hyp-20261001-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Iterative shared divider\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The measured critical path runs through forwarding, EX, and the ALU, and the current ALU contains four combinational divide/remainder operators. Their long arithmetic cones can dominate timing even when the current instruction is not a divide.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The measured critical path runs through forwarding, EX, and the ALU, and the current ALU contains four combinational divide/remainder operators. Their long arithmetic cones can dominate timing even when the current instruction is not a divide.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Move DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU into a shared radix-2 iterative execution unit that performs one quotient bit per cycle. Interlock the in-order pipeline while the unit runs and return the completed quotient or remainder through EX/MEM. This removes the deep combinational divider from the ordinary EX datapath, which should raise Fmax substantially; the cycle penalty is limited to divide/remainder instructions. Preserve RV32M corner cases, including divide by zero and signed overflow.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 12, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove combinational divide and remainder operators from the main ALU path and route these operations to the iterative unit.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Start and collect iterative divide/remainder operations while holding the executing instruction until its result is ready.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Coordinate divider busy/complete interlocking with fetch, decode, and downstream pipeline state.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend pipeline stall control for multicycle divide/remainder execution without breaking memory-stall or redirect handling.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/divider.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a shared 32-step signed/unsigned iterative divider producing quotient and remainder with RV32M semantics.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\n…[25055 of 28127 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:8f3c3ee92d1e7f77]…\n.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 106.62, \"delta_pct\": -0.9, \"vs_baseline\": 779.7, \"fmax_mhz\": 50.981, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4781572, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 2543, \"ff\": 665, \"seeds\": [48.309, 50.981, 50.981], \"perturbations\": [[0, 48.309, 13], [1, 50.981, 13], [2, 50.981, 13]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0\", \"to\": \"dmem_1_dmem_1_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -15.7, \"arrival_ns\": 25.995, \"logic_cells\": 13, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 13, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T06:06:51.703029Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 8, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-002-r8s1 (regression, -0.90%): A one-entry registered IF/ID boundary keeps issue single-width but adds payload flops and redirect/stall coordination, and this CoreMark regression shows fetch/decode retiming alone did not repay those costs here.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
