{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_5", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\np='cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'\nfor line in open(p):\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d.get('id') in ['hyp-20261001-003-r7s2','hyp-20261001-003-r8s2','hyp-20261001-003-r9s2']:\n  print('\\\\n###',d['id'],d['title'])\n  print(d['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\n  print('changes:')\n  for c in d['changes']: print(c)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "\n### hyp-20261001-003-r7s2 Single-entry loop branch predictor\nAdd a single-entry tagged predictor for backward conditional branches. Train\nits PC tag, resolved target, and saturating direction counter from EX; on a\ntag hit in IF, use the stored target when the counter predicts taken and\ncarry prediction metadata with the instruction. EX corrects fetch only on a\nprediction mismatch. A single register entry avoids indexed BTB storage and\nremoves immediate decoding and target addition from the predicted-taken\nfetch path, while recurrent loop branches can benefit from fewer redirects.\n\nchanges:\n{'file': 'rtl/core_pkg.sv', 'description': 'Carry branch prediction validity, direction, and target from fetch to EX.'}\n{'file': 'rtl/if_stage.sv', 'description': 'Add a single tagged target/counter entry and use it for predicted-taken fetches.'}\n{'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': 'Expose resolved backward-branch training information and correct prediction mismatches.'}\n{'file': 'rtl/core.sv', 'description': 'Connect resolved branch training signals from EX to the IF predictor.'}\n\n### hyp-20261001-003-r8s2 Tiny bimodal predictor for loop branches\nAdd a four-entry, two-bit saturating direction table indexed by low branch-PC\nbits, updated when conditional branches resolve in EX. Consult it only for\nlegal backward conditional branches in fetch; a taken prediction selects\nthe target formed from that instruction's B-immediate, while all other\ninstructions predict sequential execution. Carry the predicted direction\nwith the branch and let EX redirect only on a mismatch. The compact table\navoids BTB tags and 32-bit target storage, while learned direction should\nreduce loop-exit and irregular-branch mispredictions compared with a fixed\nbackward-taken rule.\n\nchanges:\n{'file': 'rtl/core_pkg.sv', 'description': 'Carry branch prediction metadata from fetch into branch resolution.'}\n{'file': 'rtl/if_stage.sv', 'description': 'Add the small direction table and use backward-branch predictions with the immediate target.'}\n{'file': 'rtl/id_stage.sv', 'description': 'Preserve prediction metadata alongside the decoded branch.'}\n{'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': 'Update the direction table from resolved branches and redirect on prediction mismatch.'}\n{'file': 'rtl/core.sv', 'description': 'Connect branch resolution training signals to the fetch predictor.'}\n\n### hyp-20261001-003-r9s2 Shared loop direction predictor\nAdd one global two-bit saturating counter, initialized weakly taken and\nupdated by each resolved conditional branch. In fetch, only legal backward\nconditional branches consult this counter; when it predicts taken, use the\nbranch immediate target, and otherwise continue sequentially. Carry the\nprediction bit with the instruction and have EX redirect only when the\nactual outcome differs. The shared state removes table indexing and tag\ncomparisons from the predictor while adapting to loop exits, which may\nimprove on fixed backward-taken prediction without the area and lookup cost\nof multi-entry direction tables.\n\nchanges:\n{'file': 'rtl/core_pkg.sv', 'description': 'Carry predicted branch direction from fetch through ID/EX.'}\n{'file': 'rtl/if_stage.sv', 'description': 'Add a shared saturating direction counter and use it for backward branch predictions.'}\n{'file': 'rtl/id_stage.sv', 'description': 'Preserve prediction metadata alongside each fetched instruction.'}\n{'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': 'Update the shared counter from resolved branches and correct direction mispredictions.'}\n{'file': 'rtl/core.sv', 'description': 'Connect resolved branch outcomes to fetch predictor training.'}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
