{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-003-r7s2.yaml <<'EOF'\nid: hyp-20261001-003-r7s2\ntitle: \\\"Single-entry loop branch predictor\\\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  Prior predictors lost fitness after adding multi-entry lookup, early branch\n  resolution, or immediate target addition to the fetch path. CoreMark repeats\n  loop branches, so a tiny predictor that caches one resolved backward branch's\n  target could avoid recurring redirect bubbles with much less table logic.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a single-entry tagged predictor for backward conditional branches. Train\n  its PC tag, resolved target, and saturating direction counter from EX; on a\n  tag hit in IF, use the stored target when the counter predicts taken and\n  carry prediction metadata with the instruction. EX corrects fetch only on a\n  prediction mismatch. A single register entry avoids indexed BTB storage and\n  removes immediate decoding and target addition from the predicted-taken\n  fetch path, while recurrent loop branches can benefit from fewer redirects.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \\\"Carry branch prediction validity, direction, and target from fetch to EX.\\\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \\\"Add a single tagged target/counter entry and use it for predicted-taken fetches.\\\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \\\"Expose resolved backward-branch training information and correct prediction mismatches.\\\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \\\"Connect resolved branch training signals from EX to the IF predictor.\\\"\nEOF\ncat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-003-r7s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
