{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_32","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"git status --short && git diff --check && test -f cores/bench/implementation_notes.md && sed -n '1,80p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/core.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/mem_stage.sv\n# Implementation notes\n\n- Added a one-entry posted-store buffer in `rtl/mem_stage.sv`. An empty buffer allows a store to leave MEM immediately; if the bus is stalled, its aligned address, replicated write data, and byte enables are captured and held until `dmemReady`.\n- MEM selects the buffered request ahead of younger traffic. It stalls a load until an older buffered store drains and stalls a later store until the entry is free. Independent instructions continue while a posted store waits.\n- Routed MEM's ordering/backpressure decision into the existing hazard control. The core interface and NRET=1 RVFI shape are unchanged.\n- The implementation follows the proposed design. Store bus addresses are word-aligned, matching the byte-lane mask and the data-memory word indexing.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Verilator lint: passed.\n- Formal: passed, 53 checks and 0 failures. `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh` selected the single-retire wrapper and checks from `core.yaml`.\n- Cosim: passed with `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench` (`selftest` and CoreMark). A first unqualified `make cosim TARGET=bench` did not reach simulation because the build script defaults to `NRET=2`, which references channel-1 RVFI ports absent by this core's declared `nret: 1` contract.\n- Gowin timing: unable to complete; synthesis stopped while inferring `dmem_3` because 16,384 DFFs exceed the device limit of 15,750. No Fmax report was produced.\n\n## Concerns\n\n- Stores can retire at enqueue time, before the external memory accepts them. Loads and younger stores are ordered behind the buffer; other instructions may pass it as intended.\n- The required cosim run validated randomized stalls and CoreMark CRCs. The default make invocation needs `NRET=1` for this target.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
